    "method_template:rack::app::ModuleWidget::getModule<type>()": {
      "finding": "The pinned API surface declares this template with a TModule type parameter. bindings/generated/mapping.json maps it to rackpy.raw.app.ModuleWidget.get_module, but native/bindings/app/module_widget.cpp binds a parameterless getter returning a generic engine Module; src/rackpy/raw/app.pyi likewise declares only get_module() -> Module | None. tests/app/in_rack/test_module_widget.py checks only the parameterless getter. The template's typed result/class selection is not represented. docs/coverage.md policy 10 requires templates over widget or module types to map to factories accepting a class, including Python subclasses.",
      "verdict": "finding"
    },
